% English break decisions, over the stock patterns of hyph_en_US.dic.
%
% Liang patterns are generated from a word list by machine and are judged on
% aggregate. That is the right way to cover a language, but it takes no view of
% how often a word is read, and the commonest few hundred words of English are
% on every page of every book. A division that reads poorly in one of those is
% seen constantly, so those words are decided one at a time here.
%
% Two rules produced the list, applied to the English vocabulary of this
% library ranked by how often each word occurs.
%
%   1. A word of five letters or fewer is not divided at all — the division
%      would save less than it costs to read. This is MINWORDLENGTH below and
%      is the rule the Oxford style manuals state.
%
%   2. A division that leaves two letters is kept only where those two letters
%      are a unit of the word: a prefix (re-turn, ex-plain, in-stead), a word
%      in its own right (my-self, no-body, an-other), or the first half of a
%      doubled consonant (of-fice, ap-pear, ac-count). Where they are instead
%      the opening syllable of a stem that means nothing without the rest, the
%      division is dropped: the reader is left holding a fragment that carries
%      no sense, for the width of two letters.
%
% Dropping such a division moves it to the next place the word divides, or
% leaves the word whole where there is no other. Both groups are below.

MINWORDLENGTH 6

% Divided later, off the opening: the word is built on a stem or a part
% that the stock division cuts through.
activ-i-ties
activ-ity
actu-ally
